readme_title = md`# SoundScript

This module is the SoundScript language: the checker, the compiler from a checked cell to runtime variables, the library those variables call, and the editor support. It does not need the tutorial module; a notebook can keep this one and drop the other.

Four SoundScript cells and a view that uses them:`
// %%
//ss-cards: ./core-example.ts
// %%
example_view = htl.html`<div class="ss-example"><button onclick=${() => bump()}>bump</button> <button onclick=${() => reset()}>reset</button> <code>tally = ${tally}</code>, <code>doubled = ${doubled}</code></div>`
// %%
readme_example = md`\`tally\` is state. \`bump\` and \`reset\` are actions, the only places it is written. \`doubled\` reads it. Open any of them with its **edit** bar; an edit is always stored; a cell that does not check does not run.`
// %%
readme_use = ss_highlightCode(md`## Using it in a module

To write SoundScript cells in another module of this notebook, import \`ss\` and each capability your cells name:

\`\`\`
import { ss, ss_now, ss_random, ss_log, ss_fetch, ss_pool } from "@tomlarkworthy/soundscript"
\`\`\`

Every compiled cell takes \`ss\` as its first input. Add a cell in the editor and type a source that starts with \`export\`, such as \`export const total = (a: number, b: number) => a + b;\`. In a module that has \`ss\`, the editor treats that source as SoundScript: it checks it against the module's other SoundScript cells and, if it is \`ok\`, compiles and defines it. A module whose cells call \`compile\` also defines \`ss_compile\`:

\`\`\`
ss_compile = ss.compiler(() => ss_source(my_module))
viewof my_module = thisModule()   // from @tomlarkworthy/runtime-sdk
\`\`\``)
// %%
readme_capabilities = md`## Capabilities

A capability parameter becomes an input on one of this module's variables:

| parameter | variable |
|---|---|
| \`now\` | \`ss_now\` |
| \`random\` | \`ss_random\` |
| \`fetch\` | \`ss_fetch\` |
| \`log\` | \`ss_log\` |
| \`pool\` | \`ss_pool\` (workers start on first use) |
| \`compile\` | \`ss_compile\`, defined by the module that uses it |
| \`invalidation\` | the runtime's own \`invalidation\` |`
// %%
readme_storage = md`## How a cell is recognised and stored

A cell compiles to ordinary JavaScript: one runtime variable, or two for a ref cell. In a ref cell, \`viewof tally\` holds the handle and \`tally\` holds the value. The \`viewof\` name makes the notebook's tools group the pair as one cell.

A variable is SoundScript when its definition is an arrow function whose body starts with the marker \`/*{lang:"ss"}*/\`. The definition keeps the types as \`/*ss:…*/\` comments. It keeps JSX as \`/*ss<…*/\` comments beside the lowered \`h(...)\` calls. The typed source is therefore recovered from the definition text alone, and it survives a save (\`test_ss_roundtrip\`).`
// %%
readme_memo = md`## When a cell does not run

\`ss.cell\` memoises on \`id\`, a hash of the compiled text. The compiler writes \`id\` into the definition. When every input is the same value (\`Object.is\`) as on the last run, the body does not run.

An edit starts with an empty memo. Two cells with equal text and equal inputs share a result; this is sound because both compute the same value.

The compiler sets \`memo: true\` only on a plain cell that the checker accepts over its whole module (\`ss_context\`). It never sets it on a generator, on a reader of a generator that is not taken as \`Events\`, or on a cell taking \`now\`, \`random\`, \`fetch\` or \`log\`. A rejected cell does not run: its definition only raises the checker's messages.`
// %%
readme_editing = md`## Editing

\`ss_registration\` registers the language with the editor through the plugin point \`cell_languages\`. Only this notebook's copy of \`@tomlarkworthy/editor-5\` has that plugin point.

For a cell whose variables carry the marker, the editor shows the typed source. It reports the checker's diagnostics as you type. What the edit does to other cells is shown on its first line: the cells it breaks, blocks or repairs, and after Shift-Enter the cells it broke, blocked or repaired.

Shift-Enter stores the edit whatever the checker says, unless it names no cell or another cell's name. A cell that is not \`ok\` compiles to a definition that raises the checker's messages, with its typed source kept in the marker comment. A stored edit compiles again any other cell whose compiled form it changes. \`ss_lifecycle\` does the same for a change made outside the editor, such as a deleted cell.`
// %%
readme_limits = md`## Limits

- The editor hook needs the \`cell_languages\` plugin point, which only this notebook's copy of \`@tomlarkworthy/editor-5\` has. Running these cells with another editor was not tried.
- A cell that does not parse is stored only if its text starts with \`export const <name>\`; otherwise there is no name to store it under.
- A module holds one source file's worth of cells. Unchecked shell cells and trusted foreign declarations, which the checker can read, are not supported here.
- The renderer's event decoding and \`ss.mount\` are outside the checked language.
- Publishing these modules to ObservableHQ was not tried.`
// %%
readme_api = ss_highlightCode(md`## API

\`\`\`
ss.checkSources({ cells, tsx })        // the checker: per cell {name, status, errors, unsupported, value (its type)}
ss.check(source, tsx = true)           // checkSources, remembered for the last 16 sources; .facts per cell (not enumerable)
ss.compileCell(source, tsx, context)   // one cell's source -> [{name, inputs, definition}]; context: ss_context(module texts)
ss.decompileVariable(definition)       // a compiled definition -> the cell's source, or null
ss.compiler(() => source)              // the value of ss_compile: compile(...) for the cells of that source
ss.evals(variable._definition)         // how many times a compiled cell's body has run
ss.running()                           // listeners attached on the page
ss.pulling()                           // events cells whose generator is being pulled
ss.release(value)                      // a deleted variable's listener ends, or its events stop
ss.forget(definition)                  // drop a compiled definition's memo entry and run count
ss.memoSize(), ss.memoHas(id)          // memo entries on the page; whether one id has one
ss.idOf(definition), ss.withId(definition, id)  // read or replace a compiled definition's memo id
ss_moduleCells(module)                 // a module's SoundScript cells: [{key, text, variable}]
ss_source(module)                      // those cells' source, joined in runtime order
ss_check(module)                       // checkSources over ss_source(module)
ss_roundtrip(module)                   // decompile and recompile every cell; throws on a difference
ss_language                            // the object registered with the editor
ss_instance(module, invalidation)      // a second, unseen copy of module's SoundScript cells, for tests
ss_card(module, name, invalidation)    // a card: the cell's typed source, its check, type and value
ss_listing(module, invalidation)       // all of a module's SoundScript source, as its cells are now
ss_tests_on                            // pending until "run the tests" is on; test cells take it as an input
\`\`\``)
// %%
ss = {
  const stream = (await FileAttachment("ss.js.gz").stream()).pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream("gzip"));
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([await new Response(stream).text()], { type: "text/javascript" }));
  try {
    return await import(url);
  } finally {
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
  }
}
// %%
ss_now = () => performance.now()
// %%
ss_random = Math.random
// %%
ss_log = (...args) => console.log(...args)
// %%
ss_fetch = globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis)
// %%
viewof ss_module = thisModule()
// %%
ss_keyOf = (name) => (name.startsWith("type ") ? name : name.replace(/^viewof /, ""))
// %%
ss_moduleCells = (module) => {
  // runtime order, one entry per cell: a ref cell's two variables give one
  const out = [], seen = new Set();
  for (const v of runtime._variables) {
    if (v._module !== module || typeof v._name !== "string" || typeof v._definition !== "function") continue;
    const def = String(v._definition);
    if (ss.langOf(def) !== "ss") continue;
    let text = ss.decompileVariable(def);
    if (text === null) continue;
    const key = ss_keyOf(v._name);
    // a compiled definition copied under another name (bump_copy) decompiles to the original's name;
    // the variable's own name wins, so recompiling it never defines a second bump
    if (!key.startsWith("type ")) {
      const head = /^((?:\s*(?:\/\/[^\n]*|\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\/))*\s*export\s+(?:const|let|function\*?)\s+)([\w$]+)/.exec(text);
      if (head && head[2] !== key) text = head[1] + key + text.slice(head[0].length);
    }
    if (seen.has(key)) continue;
    seen.add(key);
    out.push({ key, text, variable: v });
  }
  return out;
}
// %%
ss_check = (module) => {
  // one check of the module; a cell that does not parse is checked as a stand-in (ss.checkCells)
  const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
  const { result } = ss.checkCells(cells.map((c) => c.text));
  return { cells, source: cells.map((c) => c.text).join("\n\n"), result, states: ss.cellStates(result) };
}
// %%
ss_context = (texts) => {
  // the compile context of a module's cells, from one (remembered) check of the whole module: which
  // cells are generators, which are taken as Events, which the checker accepts (only those run, and
  // only those are memoised; any other cell compiles to a definition that raises the checker's messages)
  return ss.contextFromCheck(ss.checkCells(texts).result);
}
// %%
ss_source = (module) => ss_moduleCells(module).map((c) => c.text).join("\n\n")
// %%
ss_roundtrip = (module) => {
  let n = 0;
  const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
  const ctx = ss_context(cells.map((c) => c.text));
  for (const c of cells) {
    for (const d of ss.compileCell(c.text, true, ctx, c.key)) {
      const v = module._scope.get(d.name);
      if (!v) throw new Error(`${d.name}: no variable`);
      if (String(v._definition) !== d.definition) throw new Error(`${d.name}: the definition does not recompile to itself`);
      if (JSON.stringify(v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)) !== JSON.stringify(d.inputs)) throw new Error(`${d.name}: inputs ${v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)} vs ${d.inputs}`);
      n++;
    }
  }
  return n;
}
// %%
ss_pool = ss.lazyPool()
// %%
ss_instances = new WeakSet()
// %%
ss_deleted = {
  // A deleted variable's listener ends, or its events stop, once: the runtime does not resolve a
  // deleted variable's invalidation, and one deletion reaches both apply and onCodeChange.
  const done = new WeakSet();
  return (v) => { if (done.has(v)) return; done.add(v); ss.release(v._value); };
}
// %%
ss_instance = async (module, invalidation) => {
  // A second copy of module's SoundScript cells in a module of its own, so a test drives its own refs
  // and listeners, not the ones on the page. Ids get a suffix, so its memo and run counts are its
  // own too. Inputs its cells do not define (ss, ss_now, ...) are read from module. Deleted on invalidation.
  const vars = [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === module && typeof v._name === "string" && typeof v._definition === "function" && ss.langOf(String(v._definition)) === "ss");
  const names = new Set(vars.map((v) => v._name));
  const outside = new Set(vars.flatMap((v) => v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)).filter((n) => !names.has(n) && n !== "invalidation"));
  const tag = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);
  const fns = await realize(vars.map((v) => { const def = String(v._definition), id = ss.idOf(def); return id ? ss.withId(def, `${id}_${tag}`) : def; }), runtime);
  const inst = runtime.module();
  ss_instances.add(inst);
  for (const n of outside) inst.define(n, [], () => module.value(n));
  const made = vars.map((v, i) => inst.define(v._name, v._inputs.map((x) => x._name), fns[i]));
  const cancels = made.map((v) => observe(v, {}));
  invalidation.then(() => { cancels.forEach((c) => c()); for (const v of [...runtime._variables]) if (v._module === inst) { ss_deleted(v); ss.forget(v._definition); v.delete(); } });
  return inst;
}
// %%
ss_lifecycle = {
  // Edits made outside apply (the editor's delete button, another tool) reach a module through
  // onCodeChange, which diffs snapshots of the runtime's variables. A variable added and deleted
  // between two snapshots produces no event of its own, so on any SoundScript change the whole
  // module is recompiled to its fixpoint (settle), and listeners and events that no variable holds
  // any more are stopped (sweep). The runtime does not resolve a deleted variable's invalidation.
  const isSs = (v) => typeof v?._definition === "function" && ss.langOf(String(v._definition)) === "ss";
  let scheduled = false;
  const touched = new Set();
  const off = onCodeChange(({ variable, previous }) => {
    const module = variable?._module ?? previous?._module;
    if (!isSs(variable) && !isSs(previous)) return;
    if (variable === null) ss_deleted(previous.variable);
    // every edit gives a new memo id; the old one is forgotten once no variable has that definition
    if (isSs(previous) && previous._definition !== variable?._definition) {
      const text = String(previous._definition);
      if (![...runtime._variables].some((x) => x._definition && String(x._definition) === text)) ss.forget(previous._definition);
    }
    if (module?._scope?.has("ss") && !ss_instances.has(module)) touched.add(module);
    if (scheduled) return;
    scheduled = true;
    queueMicrotask(() => {
      scheduled = false;
      ss.sweep(new Set([...runtime._variables].map((x) => x._value)));
      ss.listenerOrderChanged();
      for (const m of touched) ss_language.settle(m).catch((e) => console.error(e));
      touched.clear();
    });
  });
  // where a listener's cell is, for the order listeners of one events cell run in: its module's name
  // and its place among that module's variables, which is the order the module is saved in
  const unnamed = new WeakMap();
  const nameOf = (m) => { for (const [n, x] of runtime.mains ?? []) if (x === m) return n; if (!unnamed.has(m)) unnamed.set(m, `~${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)}`); return unnamed.get(m); };
  ss.setListenerOrder((values) => {
    const want = new Set(values), at = new Map(), seen = new Map();
    for (const v of runtime._variables) {
      const n = (seen.get(v._module) ?? 0) + 1;
      seen.set(v._module, n);
      if (want.has(v._value) && !at.has(v._value)) at.set(v._value, [v._module, n]);
    }
    return values.map((x) => { const p = at.get(x); return p ? [nameOf(p[0]), p[1]] : null; });
  });
  invalidation.then(() => { off(); ss.setListenerOrder(null); });
  return "a change outside apply recompiles its module and stops listeners and events no variable holds";
}
// %%
ss_language = {
  const tsx = true;
  const isSs = (v) => typeof v?._definition === "function" && ss.langOf(String(v._definition)) === "ss";
  const keyOf = ss_keyOf;
  const moduleOf = (variables, cell) => variables.find((v) => v?._module)?._module ?? cell?.module?.module;
  const family = (module, key) => (key.startsWith("type ") ? [key] : [key, ss.handleName(key)]).map((n) => module?._scope?.get(n)).filter(isSs);
  const ownKey = (variables) => { const v = variables.find(isSs); return v ? keyOf(v._name) : null; };
  const sourceOf = (v) => ss.decompileVariable(String(v._definition));

  const decompile = async (variables) => {
    for (const v of variables) if (isSs(v)) { const s = sourceOf(v); if (s !== null) return s; }
    // a ref cell's value variable holds no source; its handle variable does
    const key = ownKey(variables);
    for (const v of family(moduleOf(variables), key)) { const s = sourceOf(v); if (s !== null) return s; }
    throw new Error(`no SoundScript source for ${key}`);
  };

  // what storing an edit does to the other cells: those ok now that would not be, and the reverse
  const plural = (n) => `${n} cell${n === 1 ? "" : "s"}`;
  // (breaks: ok before, rejected after; blocks: ok before, blocked after; repairs: not ok before, ok after)
  const effectOf = (before, after) => {
    const was = (n, f) => before.has(n) && f(before.get(n).state);
    const breaks = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "rejected" && was(n, (s) => s === "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    const blocks = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "blocked" && was(n, (s) => s === "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    const repairs = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "ok" && was(n, (s) => s !== "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    return { breaks, blocks, repairs };
  };
  const sayEffect = ({ breaks, blocks, repairs }, done) => {
    const parts = [];
    if (breaks.length) parts.push(`${done ? "broke" : "breaks"} ${plural(breaks.length)}: ${breaks.join(", ")}`);
    if (blocks.length) parts.push(`${done ? "blocked" : "blocks"} ${plural(blocks.length)}: ${blocks.join(", ")}`);
    if (repairs.length) parts.push(`${done ? "repaired" : "repairs"} ${plural(repairs.length)}: ${repairs.join(", ")}`);
    return parts.length ? `${done ? "this edit" : "applying this"} ${parts.join("; ")}` : "";
  };
  // the last stored edit's effect, per module and cell, shown on that cell while its text is unchanged
  const lastEffect = new WeakMap();

  // {ok (the edited cell checks), store (Shift-Enter stores it), problems: [{line, rule, msg}] with lines
  // relative to source, effect, defs, texts, state}. Every edit is stored except one that names no cell
  // or takes the name of another cell of the module.
  const check = (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const texts = cells.map((c) => c.text);
    const oldKey = ownKey(variables);
    let at = cells.findIndex((c) => c.key === oldKey);
    if (at < 0) { texts.push(source); at = texts.length - 1; } else texts[at] = source;
    // one check of the module as edited gives the verdicts, the compile context and the cell facts
    let after = null, checkError = null;
    try { after = ss.checkCells(texts).result; } catch (e) { checkError = e; }
    if (!after) return { ok: false, store: false, problems: [{ line: 1, rule: "check", msg: `${checkError.message}; a cell that does not parse is stored only when it starts with export const <name>` }] };
    let defs;
    try { defs = ss.compileCell(source, tsx, ss.contextFromCheck(after), oldKey); }
    catch (e) { return { ok: false, store: false, problems: [{ line: e.loc?.line ?? 1, rule: "compile", msg: e.message }] }; }
    const key = keyOf(defs.at(-1).name);
    const own = new Set([...variables, ...(oldKey ? family(module, oldKey) : [])]);
    const problems = [];
    let store = true;
    for (const d of defs) {
      const there = module?._scope?.get(d.name);
      if (there && !own.has(there)) { store = false; problems.push({ line: 1, rule: "duplicate-cell", msg: `${d.name} is already defined in this module, so this edit is not stored` }); }
    }
    const start = texts.slice(0, at).reduce((n, t) => n + t.split("\n").length + 1, 0);
    const end = start + source.split("\n").length;
    const rel = (e) => ({ ...e, line: Math.max(1, e.line - start) });
    const parseMsg = after.unparsed?.get(key);
    if (parseMsg !== undefined) problems.push({ line: Number(/\((\d+):\d+\)/.exec(parseMsg)?.[1] ?? 1), rule: "parse", msg: parseMsg });
    for (const e of after.module) if (e.line > start && e.line <= end) problems.push(rel(e));
    const mine = parseMsg === undefined ? after.cells.find((c) => c.name === key) : null;
    if (mine) {
      for (const e of mine.errors) problems.push(rel(e));
      for (const u of mine.unsupported) problems.push({ ...rel(u), rule: "unsupported" });
    }
    const statesAfter = ss.cellStates(after);
    let statesBefore = new Map();
    try { statesBefore = ss.cellStates(ss.checkCells(cells.map((c) => c.text)).result); } catch {}
    const state = statesAfter.get(key) ?? { state: "rejected", why: [], blockedBy: [] };
    if (state.state === "blocked") problems.push({ line: 1, rule: "blocked", msg: `blocked by ${state.blockedBy.join(", ")}: it does not run until ${state.blockedBy.length > 1 ? "they are" : "that is"} ok` });
    const effect = sayEffect(effectOf(statesBefore, statesAfter), false);
    return { ok: problems.length === 0 && state.state === "ok", store, problems, effect, statesBefore, statesAfter, defs, key, texts, state: state.state, status: mine?.status ?? (parseMsg !== undefined ? "rejected" : null), type: mine?.value ?? null };
  };

  const lint = (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const starts = [0];
    for (let i = 0; i < source.length; i++) if (source[i] === "\n") starts.push(i + 1);
    const r = check(source, variables, cell);
    const diags = r.problems.map((p) => {
      const l = Math.min(Math.max(p.line, 1), starts.length) - 1;
      const to = l + 1 < starts.length ? starts[l + 1] - 1 : source.length;
      return { from: starts[l], to: Math.max(to, starts[l]), severity: "error", message: `[${p.rule}] ${p.msg}` };
    });
    // what applying would do to the other cells, or, once applied, what it did
    const done = r.key ? lastEffect.get(moduleOf(variables, cell))?.get(r.key) : null;
    const say = r.effect || (done && done.text === source ? done.msg : "");
    if (say) diags.push({ from: 0, to: Math.min(starts[1] ? starts[1] - 1 : source.length, source.length), severity: "info", message: say });
    return diags;
  };

  // Replaces the variables in old with defs; new variables go after anchor.
  // With a transaction tx {made, doomed}, new variables are recorded and old ones are only marked, so
  // the caller can delete them on commit or undo everything.
  const define = async (module, defs, old, anchor, tx = null) => {
    const fns = await realize(defs.map((d) => d.definition), runtime);
    const fresh = [];
    const next = defs.map((d, i) => {
      let v = module._scope.get(d.name);
      if (!v || !old.has(v)) {
        v = module.variable({});
        v.pid = "_" + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 9);
        fresh.push(v);
        tx?.made.push(v);
      }
      const was = v._definition;
      v.define(d.name, d.inputs, fns[i]);
      // a reused variable's old definition is forgotten here: onCodeChange polls, so it can miss one
      if (was && String(was) !== d.definition) forgetUnheld(was);
      return v;
    });
    // placed before the old variables go, since a deleted anchor has no position
    if (anchor && fresh.length) {
      let at = [...runtime._variables].indexOf(anchor) + 1;
      for (const v of fresh) repositionSetElement(runtime._variables, v, at++);
    }
    const drop = (v) => { ss_deleted(v); ss.forget(v._definition); v.delete(); };
    for (const v of old) if (!next.includes(v)) tx ? tx.doomed.push(v) : drop(v);
    return next;
  };
  const forgetUnheld = (definition) => {
    const text = String(definition);
    if (![...runtime._variables].some((x) => x._definition && String(x._definition) === text)) ss.forget(definition);
  };
  const same = (vs, defs) => vs.length === defs.length && defs.every((d) => {
    const v = vs.find((x) => x._name === d.name);
    return v && String(v._definition) === d.definition && JSON.stringify(v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)) === JSON.stringify(d.inputs);
  });

  // Stores the edit whatever its verdict (not stored, returning undefined: no cell name, or another
  // cell's name). A cell the checker does not accept compiles to a definition that raises its messages.
  // Every other cell whose compiled form the edit changes is compiled again too: one that becomes, or
  // stops being, accepted; a generator that became, or stopped being, taken as Events; a reader of a
  // generator, which is not memoised.
  const applyNow = async (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const r = check(source, variables, cell);
    if (!r.store) return undefined;
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const oldKey = ownKey(variables);
    // a Notebook Kit cell converted to SoundScript also takes its shadow variables (display) with it
    const old = new Set([...variables.flatMap((v) => [v, ...(v._shadow?.values() ?? [])]), ...(oldKey ? family(module, oldKey) : [])]);
    const order = [...runtime._variables];
    const anchor = [...old].sort((a, b) => order.indexOf(a) - order.indexOf(b)).at(-1) ?? cell?.variables?.at(-1);
    // every other cell whose compiled form the edit changes is compiled before anything is defined
    const ctx = ss_context(r.texts);
    const plan = [];
    for (const c of ss_moduleCells(module)) {
      if (c.key === r.key || c.key === oldKey) continue;
      const defs = ss.compileCell(c.text, tsx, ctx, c.key);
      const fam = family(module, c.key);
      if (!same(fam, defs)) plan.push({ defs, fam });
    }
    // then all of it is defined; if any step throws, every variable touched gets its old definition back
    const touchedVars = new Set([...old, ...plan.flatMap((p) => p.fam)]);
    const saved = [...touchedVars].map((v) => ({ v, name: v._name, inputs: v._inputs.map((i) => i._name), definition: v._definition }));
    const tx = { made: [], doomed: [] };
    let next;
    try {
      next = await define(module, r.defs, old, anchor, tx);
      if (faults.afterEditDefine === module) throw new Error("injected fault after the edited cell was defined");
      for (const p of plan) await define(module, p.defs, new Set(p.fam), p.fam.at(-1), tx);
    } catch (e) {
      for (const v of tx.made) v.delete();
      for (const s of saved) s.v.define(s.name, s.inputs, s.definition);
      throw e;
    }
    for (const v of new Set(tx.doomed)) { ss_deleted(v); ss.forget(v._definition); v.delete(); }
    // a reused Kit head no longer has shadows; theirs were deleted with the rest of old
    for (const v of next) v._shadow?.clear?.();
    variables.splice(0, variables.length, ...next);
    const stored = await decompile(next);
    const msg = sayEffect(effectOf(r.statesBefore, r.statesAfter), true);
    if (!lastEffect.has(module)) lastEffect.set(module, new Map());
    lastEffect.get(module).set(r.key, { text: stored, msg });
    return stored;
  };
  // test hook: set afterEditDefine to a module, and an apply there fails after defining the edited cell
  const faults = { afterEditDefine: null };
  // compiles again every cell of module (but skip) whose form the rest of the module changed
  const recompileNow = async (module, skip) => {
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const ctx = ss_context(cells.map((c) => c.text));
    let n = 0;
    for (const c of cells) {
      if (c.key === skip) continue;
      const defs = ss.compileCell(c.text, tsx, ctx, c.key);
      const fam = family(module, c.key);
      if (!same(fam, defs)) { await define(module, defs, new Set(fam), fam.at(-1)); n++; }
    }
    return n;
  };

  // completion at pos in source, with the module's other cells as context: {from, to, options, mode}
  const complete = (source, pos, variables = [], cell) => {
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const texts = cells.map((c) => c.text);
    const at0 = cells.findIndex((c) => c.key === ownKey(variables));
    const at = at0 < 0 ? texts.length : at0;
    texts[at] = source;
    return ss.completionsAt(texts, at, pos, tsx);
  };
  // the editor's header: the cell's parameters as inputs (not ss or a hidden invalidation), named outputs
  const header = (variables) => {
    const v = variables.find((x) => isSs(x) && ss.decompileVariable(String(x._definition)) !== null);
    if (!v) return null;
    const text = ss.decompileVariable(String(v._definition));
    const open = /export\s+(?:(?:const|let)\s+[\w$]+\s*=\s*(?:async\s+)?(?:function\*?\s*[\w$]*\s*)?|(?:async\s+)?function\*?\s+[\w$]+\s*)\(/.exec(text);
    const params = new Set();
    if (open) {
      let depth = 0, part = "";
      for (const ch of text.slice(open.index + open[0].length)) {
        if ("([{<".includes(ch)) depth++;
        if (")]}>".includes(ch)) { if (depth === 0) { params.add(/^\s*([\w$]+)/.exec(part)?.[1]); break; } depth--; }
        if (ch === "," && depth === 0) { params.add(/^\s*([\w$]+)/.exec(part)?.[1]); part = ""; } else part += ch;
      }
    }
    const own = new Set(variables);
    const inputs = [...new Set(variables.flatMap((x) => x._inputs))].filter((i) => !own.has(i) && params.has(String(i._name).replace(/^viewof /, "")));
    const outputs = [...new Set(variables.flatMap((x) => [...x._outputs]))].filter((o) => !own.has(o) && typeof o._name === "string" && o._name);
    return { inputs, outputs };
  };

  // a new cell is SoundScript when its module has ss, which every compiled cell takes
  const claimsSource = (source, cell) => {
    const module = cell?.module?.module;
    return !!module?._scope?.has("ss") && /^\s*(?:(?:\/\/[^\n]*|\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\/)\s*)*export\b/.test(source);
  };

  // Edits and recompiles run one at a time, so a recompile never reads a module another is halfway
  // through defining. settle(module) queues at most one pending recompile per module.
  let queue = Promise.resolve();
  const serial = (f) => { const r = queue.then(f); queue = r.catch(() => {}); return r; };
  const apply = (...a) => serial(() => applyNow(...a));
  const recompile = (module, skip) => serial(() => recompileNow(module, skip));
  const pending = new Set();
  const settle = (module) => {
    if (pending.has(module)) return queue;
    pending.add(module);
    return serial(() => { pending.delete(module); return recompileNow(module); });
  };
  return {
    id: "ss",
    claims: (variables) => variables.some(isSs),
    claimsSource,
    decompile,
    check,
    lint,
    complete,
    header,
    apply,
    faults,
    recompile,
    settle,
    extension: (codemirror) => codemirror.javascript({ typescript: true, jsx: true })
  };
}
// %%
ss_registration = {
  plugins.add("cell_languages", ss_language, { invalidation });
  return md`SoundScript is registered as the editor language \`${ss_language.id}\` (plugin \`cell_languages\`).`;
}
// %%
ss_badge = (status, text = status) => htl.html`<span class=${"lite-badge lite-badge-" + status}>${text}</span>`
// %%
ss_isStale = (e) => typeof e === "function" && e.name === "variable_stale"
// %%
ss_fmt = (v) => {
  if (typeof v === "function") return "ƒ";
  if (typeof v === "number") return Number.isNaN(v) ? "NaN" : String(v);
  if (v === undefined) return "undefined";
  if (ArrayBuffer.isView(v)) return `${v.constructor.name}(${v.length}) [${Array.from(v.slice(0, 8)).join(", ")}${v.length > 8 ? ", …" : ""}]`;
  if (v && typeof v === "object" && "tag" in v && "children" in v) return `<${v.tag || "fragment"}> element`;
  let s;
  try { s = JSON.stringify(v); } catch (e) { s = String(v); }
  return s === undefined ? String(v) : s.length > 90 ? s.slice(0, 87) + "..." : s;
}
// %%
ss_highlight = {
  // TypeScript and JSX colouring with the editor's own parser, as spans with CodeMirror's tok-* classes
  const lang = codemirror.javascript({ typescript: true, jsx: true }).language;
  return (text) => {
    const out = [];
    let at = 0;
    lezerhighlight.highlightTree(lang.parser.parse(text), lezerhighlight.classHighlighter, (from, to, cls) => {
      if (from > at) out.push(text.slice(at, from));
      const span = document.createElement("span");
      span.className = cls;
      span.textContent = text.slice(from, to);
      out.push(span);
      at = to;
    });
    if (at < text.length) out.push(text.slice(at));
    return out;
  };
}
// %%
ss_cardHub = {
  // one check of a module per code change, shared by all of its cards and listings
  const hubs = new Map();
  invalidation.then(() => { for (const h of hubs.values()) h.off(); });
  return (module) => {
    if (hubs.has(module)) return hubs.get(module);
    const subs = new Set();
    let state = null, queued = false;
    const off = onCodeChange(({ variable, previous }) => {
      if ((variable ?? previous)?._module !== module || queued) return;
      queued = true;
      queueMicrotask(() => { queued = false; state = null; for (const f of subs) f(); });
    });
    const hub = {
      off,
      state: () => state ?? (state = ss_check(module)),
      subscribe: (f) => { subs.add(f); return () => subs.delete(f); },
    };
    hubs.set(module, hub);
    return hub;
  };
}
// %%
ss_card = (module, key, invalidation) => {
  // a cell's typed source, decompiled from its live definition, with its check, type and value under it
  const hub = ss_cardHub(module);
  const code = htl.html`<pre class="lite-code">`, value = htl.html`<span class="lite-card-value">`;
  const meta = htl.html`<div class="lite-card-meta">`, msgs = htl.html`<div class="lite-card-msgs">`;
  const root = htl.html`<div class="lite-card" data-cell=${key}>${code}${meta}${msgs}</div>`;
  let text = null, variable = null, cancel = null, error, notRunning = false;
  const showValue = () => {
    value.textContent = notRunning ? "does not run" : error !== undefined ? `throws: ${error?.message ?? error}` : variable?._value === undefined ? "not computed yet" : ss_fmt(variable._value);
    value.classList.toggle("lite-throws", !notRunning && error !== undefined);
  };
  const watch = (v) => {
    cancel?.();
    variable = v;
    error = undefined;
    // the runtime keeps no error field, so an error arrives from observe or from the variable's promise
    cancel = observe(v, { fulfilled: () => { error = undefined; showValue(); }, rejected: (e) => { if (!ss_isStale(e)) { error = e; showValue(); } } });
    v._promise?.then(() => {}, (e) => { if (!ss_isStale(e) && variable === v) { error = e; showValue(); } });
  };
  const draw = () => {
    const { cells, result, states } = hub.state();
    const c = cells.find((x) => x.key === key);
    root.hidden = !c;
    if (!c) return;
    if (c.text !== text) { text = c.text; code.replaceChildren(...ss_highlight(text)); }
    const r = result.cells.find((x) => x.name === key);
    // ok, rejected (with the checker's messages) or blocked (by the cells it takes that are not ok)
    const st = states.get(key) ?? { state: "rejected", why: ["[check] not in the module's check"], blockedBy: [] };
    const status = st.state;
    root.className = `lite-card lite-${status}`;
    meta.replaceChildren(ss_badge(status, status === "blocked" ? `blocked by ${st.blockedBy.join(", ")}` : status), " ", htl.html`<code class="lite-card-type">${r?.value ?? ""}</code>`, " ", value);
    const problems = status === "rejected" ? st.why.map((w) => { const m = /^\[([^\]]+)\] ([\s\S]*)$/.exec(w); return m ? { rule: m[1], msg: m[2] } : { rule: "rejected", msg: w }; })
      : status === "blocked" ? [{ rule: "blocked", msg: `it takes ${st.blockedBy.join(", ")}, which ${st.blockedBy.length > 1 ? "are" : "is"} not ok, so it does not run` }] : [];
    msgs.replaceChildren(...problems.map((e) => htl.html`<div class="lite-err"><b>[${e.rule}]</b> ${e.msg}</div>`));
    notRunning = status !== "ok";
    const v = module._scope.get(key) ?? c.variable;
    if (v !== variable) watch(v);
    showValue();
  };
  draw();
  const unsubscribe = hub.subscribe(draw);
  invalidation.then(() => { unsubscribe(); cancel?.(); });
  return root;
}
// %%
ss_listing = (module, invalidation) => {
  // a whole module's typed source, as its cells are now
  const hub = ss_cardHub(module);
  const pre = htl.html`<pre class="lite-code lite-listing">`;
  let text = null;
  const draw = () => {
    const t = hub.state().cells.map((c) => c.text).join("\n\n");
    if (t !== text) { text = t; pre.replaceChildren(...ss_highlight(t)); }
  };
  draw();
  const unsubscribe = hub.subscribe(draw);
  invalidation.then(unsubscribe);
  return pre;
}
// %%
ss_highlightCode = (node) => {
  // colours an md cell's code blocks with ss_highlight; a fence without a language, so md fetches no highlighter
  for (const code of node.querySelectorAll("pre > code")) {
    code.classList.add("ss-hl");
    code.replaceChildren(...ss_highlight(code.textContent));
  }
  return node;
}
// %%
ss_card_css = `:root {
  --lite-ok: #2f9e44;
  --lite-bad: var(--theme-error, #d6336c);
  --lite-warn: #c98a12;
  --lite-accent: var(--theme-foreground-focus, #3b6fd8);
  /* text in these colours, mixed toward the foreground so it reads at 4.5:1 on dark and light themes */
  --lite-ok-text: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-ok) 55%, var(--theme-foreground));
  --lite-bad-text: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-bad) 55%, var(--theme-foreground));
  --lite-warn-text: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-warn) 55%, var(--theme-foreground));
  /* the theme's muted text and syntax colours, 30% toward the foreground: the light theme's own are 3.2 to 4.4:1 on a card */
  --lite-muted-text: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-foreground-muted) 70%, var(--theme-foreground));
}
.lite-err b { color: var(--lite-bad-text); }
.lite-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0 7px; border-radius: 9px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 18px; white-space: nowrap; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
.lite-badge-ok, .lite-badge-pass { color: var(--lite-ok-text); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-ok) 14%, transparent); }
.lite-badge-rejected, .lite-badge-fail { color: var(--lite-bad-text); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-bad) 14%, transparent); }
.lite-badge-unsupported, .lite-badge-blocked { color: var(--lite-warn-text); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lite-warn) 14%, transparent); }
.lite-badge-pending { color: var(--lite-muted-text); }
.lite-card { margin: 10px 0 0; border: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faint); border-left: 3px solid var(--lite-ok); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--theme-background-alt); max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
.lite-card.lite-rejected { border-left-color: var(--lite-bad); }
.lite-card.lite-unsupported, .lite-card.lite-blocked { border-left-color: var(--lite-warn); }
.lite-code { margin: 0; padding: 8px 10px; font: 13px/1.45 var(--monospace, monospace); color: var(--theme-foreground); background: none; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; tab-size: 2; }
.lite-card-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 10px; align-items: baseline; padding: 4px 10px 6px; border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faintest); font-size: 13px; }
.lite-card-type { color: var(--lite-muted-text); }
.lite-card-value { font-family: var(--monospace, monospace); overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-width: 0; }
.lite-card-value::before { content: "= "; color: var(--lite-muted-text); }
.lite-card-value.lite-throws { color: var(--lite-bad-text); }
.lite-card-msgs:empty { display: none; }
.lite-card-msgs { padding: 0 10px 8px; font-size: 13px; }
.lite-card-msgs .lite-err { margin-top: 2px; }
.lite-listing { max-height: 420px; overflow: auto; border: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faint); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--theme-background-alt); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-keyword, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-modifier, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-controlKeyword, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-operatorKeyword { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-keyword) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-string, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-string2 { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-string) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-number, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-bool, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-atom, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-null { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-literal) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-comment { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-comment) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); font-style: italic; }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-definition { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-definition) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-typeName, :is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-className { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-atom) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
:is(.lite-code, .ss-hl) .tok-propertyName { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-variable) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); }
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  /* a card's source wraps on a phone, keeping its indentation, rather than scrolling out of sight */
  .lite-card .lite-code { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
}`
// %%
ss_card_style = Object.assign(document.createElement("style"), { textContent: ss_card_css + "\n" + ss_card_rules })
// %%
style = htl.html`<style>
.ss-tests td, .ss-tests th { max-width: 28ch; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.ss-example { padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faint); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--theme-background-alt); }
</style>`
// %%
readme_tests = md`## Tests

The tests run only when **run the tests** is on, so a page that is only read spends nothing on them. Each test takes \`ss_tests_on\`, which stays pending until then; a pending test has not passed. \`test_ss_ref_handle\` presses **bump** and **reset** on a copy of this module (\`ss_instance\`), so the counter on the page keeps its count.`
// %%
viewof ss_run_tests = Inputs.toggle({ label: "run the tests" })
// %%
ss_tests_on = ss_run_tests ? true : invalidation
// %%
test_ss_roundtrip = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const n = ss_roundtrip(ss_module);
  if (n < 5) throw new Error(`${n} SoundScript variables in this module; the example alone has 5 (tally is two)`);
  return `${n} variables recompile to the same text and inputs`;
}
// %%
test_ss_example_checks = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const { result } = ss_check(ss_module);
  const want = ["tally", "bump", "reset", "doubled"];
  const got = Object.fromEntries(want.map((n) => [n, result.cells.find((c) => c.name === n)?.status]));
  if (want.some((n) => got[n] !== "ok")) throw new Error(`verdicts ${JSON.stringify(got)}`);
  return `${want.join(", ")}: ok`;
}
// %%
test_ss_unchanged_source_checks = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const v = ss_module._scope.get("bump");
  const source = await ss_language.decompile([v]);
  const r = ss_language.check(source, [v]);
  if (!r.ok || r.problems.length) throw new Error(JSON.stringify(r.problems));
  return `bump: ok, type ${r.type}`;
}
// %%
test_ss_wrong_type_is_stored_and_rejected = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // an edit the checker rejects is stored; the cell then raises the checker's message instead of running
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const original = await ss_language.decompile([inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    const source = original.replace("tally: Ref<number>", "tally: Ref<string>");
    if (source === original) throw new Error("bump has no tally: Ref<number> parameter to change");
    const r = ss_language.check(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (r.ok || !r.store || !r.problems.some((p) => p.rule === "inject-ref")) throw new Error(`check: ${JSON.stringify(r.problems)}`);
    const lint = ss_language.lint(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (!lint.some((d) => d.severity === "error")) throw new Error(`lint: ${JSON.stringify(lint)}`);
    const stored = await ss_language.apply(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (stored !== source) throw new Error(`stored ${JSON.stringify(stored)}`);
    let threw = null;
    try { await inst.value("bump"); } catch (e) { threw = e; }
    if (!/^bump does not check: \[inject-ref\]/.test(threw?.message ?? "")) throw new Error(`bump gave ${threw?.message ?? "a value"}`);
    await ss_language.apply(original, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (typeof (await inst.value("bump")) !== "function") throw new Error("bump did not come back after the repair");
    return `stored; bump raises "${threw.message.slice(0, 80)}"; repaired, it is an action again`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_breaking_edit_names_its_cells = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // before an edit is stored, the editor says which cells it would break
  const v = ss_module._scope.get("viewof tally");
  const original = await ss_language.decompile([v]);
  const source = original.replace("RefCell<number> => ref(0)", 'RefCell<string> => ref("0")');
  if (source === original) throw new Error("tally is not RefCell<number> => ref(0)");
  const r = ss_language.check(source, [v]);
  // bump, reset and doubled take tally; a cell added later that reads doubled is blocked
  if (!r.store || !/^applying this breaks 3 cells: bump, reset, doubled(; blocks \d+ cells?: [\w, ]+)?$/.test(r.effect)) throw new Error(`effect ${JSON.stringify(r.effect)}`);
  const d = r.statesAfter.get("doubled");
  if (d.state !== "rejected" || !d.why.some((w) => w.includes("string is not assignable to number"))) throw new Error(`doubled ${JSON.stringify(d)}`);
  const back = ss_language.check(original, [v]);
  if (back.effect !== "") throw new Error(`the unchanged source reports ${JSON.stringify(back.effect)}`);
  return r.effect;
}
// %%
test_ss_copy_keeps_its_name = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // a definition copied under another name recompiles under the copy's own name, not the original's
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const bump = inst._scope.get("bump");
    inst.variable({}).define("bump_copy", bump._inputs.map((i) => i._name), bump._definition);
    const text = ss_moduleCells(inst).find((c) => c.key === "bump_copy")?.text ?? "";
    if (!text.startsWith("export const bump_copy ")) throw new Error(`bump_copy decompiles as ${text.slice(0, 40)}`);
    await ss_language.recompile(inst);
    const named = (n) => [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === inst && v._name === n).length;
    if (named("bump") !== 1 || named("bump_copy") !== 1) throw new Error(`bump ${named("bump")}, bump_copy ${named("bump_copy")}`);
    await Promise.all([inst.value("bump"), inst.value("bump_copy")]);
    return "bump_copy recompiles as bump_copy; one bump";
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_failed_apply_changes_nothing = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // apply defines the edit and every cell it recompiles, or none of them
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  const snap = (m) => JSON.stringify([...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === m).map((v) => [v._name, String(v._definition), v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)]));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const v = inst._scope.get("viewof tally");
    const source = (await ss_language.decompile([v])).replace("ref(0)", "ref(5)");
    if (!ss_language.check(source, [v]).ok) throw new Error("the edit to tally does not check");
    const before = snap(inst);
    ss_language.faults.afterEditDefine = inst;
    let threw = null;
    try { await ss_language.apply(source, [v]); } catch (e) { threw = e; } finally { ss_language.faults.afterEditDefine = null; }
    if (!threw) throw new Error("the injected fault did not reach apply's caller");
    if (snap(inst) !== before) throw new Error("a failed apply left the module changed");
    return `the injected fault "${threw.message}" left the module as it was`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_edits_do_not_grow_the_memo = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // each edit gives the cell a new memo id; the old id's entry and run count are forgotten
  if (typeof ss.memoHas !== "function") throw new Error("ss.memoHas is missing");
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const edit = async (k) => {
      const v = inst._scope.get("doubled");
      const source = (await ss_language.decompile([v])).replace(/tally \* \d+/, `tally * ${k}`);
      if (await ss_language.apply(source, [v]) === undefined) throw new Error(`edit ${k} was not stored`);
      if ((await inst.value("doubled")) !== (await inst.value("tally")) * k) throw new Error(`doubled is not tally * ${k}`);
      await new Promise((r) => queueMicrotask(r));
    };
    // other tests run at the same time and add entries of their own, so the edited cell's ids are counted
    const ids = [];
    for (let k = 3; k < 203; k++) { await edit(k); ids.push(ss.idOf(String(inst._scope.get("doubled")._definition))); }
    const kept = ids.filter((id) => ss.memoHas(id));
    if (new Set(ids).size !== ids.length) throw new Error("two edits gave one memo id");
    if (kept.length !== 1 || kept[0] !== ids.at(-1)) throw new Error(`after 200 edits ${kept.length} of their memo ids are kept: ${kept.slice(0, 5)}`);
    return `200 edits of doubled: only the last one's memo entry is kept`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_instance_keeps_user_ids = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // ss_instance gives the copy's memo ids a suffix; a cell's own \`id:\` property is left as written
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const a = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const anchor = a._scope.get("doubled");
    const made = await ss_language.apply('export const tagged = () => ({ id: "anon", n: 1 });', [], { module: { module: a }, variables: [anchor] });
    if (made === undefined) throw new Error("tagged was not stored");
    const b = await ss_instance(a, done);
    const value = await b.value("tagged");
    const ida = ss.idOf(String(a._scope.get("tagged")._definition)), idb = ss.idOf(String(b._scope.get("tagged")._definition));
    if (value.id !== "anon" || !idb || idb === ida || !idb.startsWith(ida + "_")) throw new Error(`value ${JSON.stringify(value)}, ids ${ida} -> ${idb}`);
    return `tagged keeps id "anon"; its memo id ${ida} became ${idb}`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
//raw: test_ss_ref_handle
// %%
ss_test_results = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // a long value (an error message) is cut to one line, so the state column stays in view
  return htl.html`<div class="ss-tests">${tests({ filter: (t) => t.name.includes("@tomlarkworthy/soundscript#") })}</div>`;
}
